This suite imports your app's traced entrypoint DIRECTLY (no HTTP) and drives it through
DeepEval's evals_iterator(), which walks every @observe'd span your app
declared metrics on (e.g. a retrieve span, a generate_answer span) and
scores each one separately. This one tells you WHICH stage regressed;
the e2e one tells you whether the app's final answer is still good.

Requirements on the app side (plain DeepEval tracing, no judge, no metrics):
  - the stages you want scored are functions decorated with @observe
    (e.g. `retrieve`, `generate_answer`), called by the entrypoint below;
  - each of them calls update_current_span(test_case=LLMTestCase(...))
    with what it saw/produced (input, retrieval_context, actual_output).

The METRICS are attached here, by span name (SPAN_METRICS below), after
the app ran   so production code never imports a judge   and spans that
get metrics receive the golden's expected_output for reference-based
metrics, so the app never sees the reference answer either.

